INT. GENERATION SHIP "HALCYON" - SEED VAULT - NIGHT CYCLE

A long white corridor lined with frost-skinned drawers. Each is labeled in small black type: wheat, barley, lentil, cacao. Cold exhales from the vents. A low pump hum.

ENGINEER AKINYI WAMBUGU, 40s, thermal gloves, a utility belt, checks a sensor panel. ARCHIVIST VOSS, 50s, a cardigan too thin for the temperature, stands at the end of the aisle holding a slim black case against her chest.

AKINYI
You're not on the roster.

VOSS
I'm the Archivist. I'm always on the roster.

AKINYI
Not for this deck. Not at this hour.

Voss does not answer. She walks the aisle, running her fingertips along the frosted drawers. Akinyi watches the case.

AKINYI (CONT'D)
That's a lot of case for a woman who inventories paper.

VOSS
It's only an old habit.

AKINYI
Show me.

Voss stops at a drawer marked SOLANUM TUBEROSUM. Pulls the handle. A tray of small grey tubers slides out under glass. She sets the case on the counter. Clicks the lock. Does not open it.

VOSS
You know what we've lost in four generations, Akinyi?

AKINYI
Eleven strains of rice. Three of coffee.

VOSS
Four hundred and six varieties. I counted every one.

She slides the case a few centimeters toward the potatoes. Akinyi's eyes flick to the panel. The temperature reading has not changed. Neither has her breathing.

AKINYI
So what's in the case?

VOSS
Things the Council doesn't want to be counted.

AKINYI
That's contraband.

VOSS
That's a library.

Akinyi pulls a data slate from her belt. Taps it. A tone sounds in the ceiling.

VOSS (CONT'D)
(very quiet)
You just called them.

AKINYI
I called the Captain. He asked me to.

Voss nods. Slow. Her hand lifts from the case, rests flat on the cold metal beside it.

VOSS
Then do it. Open the drawer. Put it all in the shredder. Four hundred and six.

AKINYI
I can't.

VOSS
You can. You're holding the key.

Akinyi looks down. In her palm, a brass key. She does not know when she took it from her belt.

AKINYI
You knew I'd bring it.

VOSS
I knew you'd bring it.

The vents shudder. Steam rolls along the floor. Footsteps, far off. Many.

Akinyi lays the key on the counter, next to the case, carefully, as though it were something alive.

AKINYI
Then you've got four minutes.

Voss opens the case.
